{"name":"Lager","hex":"#f6f513","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lager","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of beer, brewed using a bottom-fermenting yeast."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To store (lager beer) at a low temperature for maturing and clarification."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lager"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lager","blocks":[{"text":"Lager is a style of beer brewed and conditioned at low temperature. Lagers can be pale, amber, or dark. Pale lager is the most widely consumed and commercially available style of beer. The term lager comes from the German word for 'storage', as the beer was stored before drinking, traditionally in the same cool caves in which it was fermented."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Bitburger_Glass.JPG/330px-Bitburger_Glass.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lager","wikidata":"Q253481"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Pilsener_Urquell_hohes_Glas.jpg/500px-Pilsener_Urquell_hohes_Glas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Pilsener_Urquell_hohes_Glas.jpg/1280px-Pilsener_Urquell_hohes_Glas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Pilsener_Urquell_hohes_Glas.jpg/500px-Pilsener_Urquell_hohes_Glas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Czech lager","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APilsener_Urquell_hohes_Glas.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Pilsner_urquell_mug.jpg/500px-Pilsner_urquell_mug.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Pi